findings.suggested_fix:
Branch on the input representation instead of always shifting. Assumption: numbers are UTC-midnight ms from Python; strings are local dates from toDateString(). E.g.

_unlocal_date(value: string | number): Date {
  const date = new Date(value)
  if (typeof value === "number")
    return new Date(date.getUTCFullYear(), date.getUTCMonth(), date.getUTCDate())
  return new Date(date.getFullYear(), date.getMonth(), date.getDate())
}

and call it as this._unlocal_date(this.model.value) etc. (ISO-only strings like "2019-09-20" set from BokehJS would parse as UTC and need a regex branch if they are to be supported). Verified in node: correct date for both representations in UTC, Europe/Paris, America/Los_Angeles, Pacific/Kiritimati, Pacific/Pago_Pago.
